      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_369855d0",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: what_do_you_mean_being_funny_isn_t_just_saying_hoes_mad; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image features a Shiba Inu dog with a skeptical or confused expression, overlaid with text that reads, 'what do you mean being funny isn't just saying hoes mad?'. The meme uses the dog's expression to convey disbelief or challenge toward the notion that humor should not be limited to crude or misogynistic content. While the meme does not target any specific individual or group based on protected characteristics, it promotes a harmful and potentially misogynistic standard of humor by equating 'funny' with objectifying or demeaning language toward women. This can normalize and legitimize sexist humor, which may contribute to a culture that devalues women and reinforces harmful stereotypes. The intent is to provoke a reaction by challenging social norms around humor, but the message itself can be seen as harmful because it implicitly condones or trivializes misogynistic behavior.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_b30dec2c"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
